B. the rank defect: min over periodic h of the worst step = max cycle mean; Collatz = log(3/2) at -1
  ok: levels 2-4, all 276 strategies: the optimal periodic correction h = (log 3/r) psi attains max over edges of (w(s) + h(t) - h(s)) = rho_max log 3 - log 2, with equality on a cycle of density rho_max
  ok: Collatz, k = 2..16: node 2^k - 1 carries the self-loop (density 1); the least potential at F = 1 is psi = 0, so h = 0 is an optimal periodic correction and the least achievable defect is exactly log(3/2) (rho_max = 1 re-derived by exact Karp for k <= 8)
  ok: the Bernoulli-boundary witnesses n_H = 2^H - 1 stay on the node -1 (mod 2^k) for H - k + 1 consecutive steps (k = 2..11, H = k..k+39): they are the integer shadow of the expanding self-loop
B'. finite banks of dyadic counters plus any periodic correction cannot pay for every expanding orbit
  ok: for a bank of 20 rational centers (incl. -1, -5, -17, -13/9, 1 - 2(4/3)^d, d <= 7) and any h mod 2^12: the Collatz orbits of 1^(L-1)0, L = 5, 7, 9, 13, 23, avoid the bank and have integer shadows n with T^L(n) > n and identical h-values and counters at n and T^L(n); so every rank a log n + h(n mod 2^12) + sum c_i v2(n - beta_i), a > 0, increases over one period
