C. the flow side: circulations, the Haar circulation, LP duality
  ok: levels 2-4 (all 276 strategies): the uniform edge flow is a circulation iff sigma is constant (Collatz or 3n-1); in-degrees always lie in {1,2,3}; Collatz is 2-in/2-out at k = 2..14, so its Haar circulation exists and has odd density exactly 1/2 (half of the nodes are odd)
  ok: levels 2-4 (276 strategies): the LP maximum of the odd density over normalized circulations equals the exact Karp rho_max (max deviation 1.1e-16; HiGHS, floating point)
